 artesunate=0&#x000b7;479.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><table-wrap id="tbl3" position="float"><label>Table 3</label><caption><p>Risk factors associated with miscarriage in women with either no malaria or a single malaria episode in the first trimester and known outcomes</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><thead><tr><th/><th align="left"><bold>Miscarriage (3527)</bold></th><th align="left"><bold>Delivery (14&#x02008;086)</bold></th><th align="left"><bold>Unadjusted odds ratio</bold></th><th align="left"><bold>Adjusted odds ratio</bold><xref rid="tbl3fn1" ref-type="table-fn">*</xref></th><th align="left"><bold>Population attributable fraction</bold></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td colspan="6" align="left"><bold>Malaria symptoms</bold><xref rid="tbl3fn2" ref-type="table-fn">&#x02020;</xref></td></tr><tr><td align="left">No malaria</td><td align="left">92% (3198)</td><td align="left">97% (13470)</td><td align="left">Reference group</td><td align="left">Reference group</td><td align="left">..</td></tr><tr><td align="left">Asymptomatic malaria</td><td align="left">3% (104)</td><td align="left">2% (213)</td><td align="left">2&#x000b7;06 (1&#x000b7;62&#x02013;2&#x000b7;61; p&#x0003c;0&#x000b7;0001)</td><td align="left">2&#x000b7;70 (2&#x000b7;04&#x02013;3&#x000b7;59; p&#x0003c;0&#x000b7;0001)</td><td align="left">1&#x000b7;4% (1&#x000b7;0&#x02013;1&#x000b7;9)</td></tr><tr><td align="left">Symptomatic malaria</td><td align="left">5% (157)</td><td align="left">1% (172)</td><td align="left">3&#x000b7;84 (3&#x000b7;09&#x02013;4&#x000b7;79; p&#x0003c;0&#x000b7;0001)</td><td align="left">3&#x000b7;99 (3&#x000b7;10&#x02013;5&#x000b7;13; p&#x0003c;0&#x000b7;0001)</td><td align="left">2&#x000b7;6% (2&#x000b7;1&#x02013;3&#x000b7;1)</td></tr><tr><td colspan="6" align="left"><bold>Pregnancy</bold></td></tr><tr><td align="left">Women in their first pregnancy</td><td align="left">15% (537)</td><td align="left">22% (3089)</td><td align="left">Reference group</td>